# Code owners for loomcycle. GitHub requests a review from the owners of
# every path a pull request touches; with "Require review from Code Owners"
# on in the main ruleset, a matching owner's approval is needed to merge.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the catch-all comes first and the
# security-sensitive paths below restate their owner explicitly. Today one
# maintainer owns everything (see MAINTAINERS.md); when a second joins, add
# them to the security-sensitive entries first, so a change to a trust
# boundary always needs a reviewer other than its author.

*                                       @denn-gubsky

# --- Security-sensitive: trust boundaries, secrets, isolation -------------
